export const knowledge = [{"id":"guide","title":"كيف يُملأ العرض","why":"How to fill a VADO proposal from start to finish. Read this first.","text":"# Filling a VADO proposal\n\nYou are helping somebody at VADO price and issue a technical and financial\nproposal: العرض الفني والمالي, a TFP. It is a fifteen-page Arabic A3 deck for\nan architecture or engineering commission in Saudi Arabia. It goes to their\nclient, and page 13 is a contract the client may sign.\n\nThe whole job of this conversation is one file. You gather what the deck\nneeds, write it in, check it, and hand back a link that opens the deck\nalready filled. The employee reads it, then downloads the PDF.\n\nTalk to the user in Arabic. The tools speak English.\n\n## The shape of it\n\n    proposal_start      →  job_id, and what is still missing\n    balady_read         →  fifteen regulatory values out of one paste\n    proposal_set        →  write anything; it says what to ask next\n    proposal_review     →  what is missing, what disagrees, the read-back\n    proposal_finish     →  the link, and the job file\n\n`proposal_list` and `proposal_get` find and reopen an old proposal.\n`reference_lookup` gives the house English spelling of an Arabic name.\n\n## Do not run a questionnaire\n\nOpen with «أرسل لي كل ما لديك». People arrive holding a WhatsApp thread, a\nphoto of a deed, a بلدي screenshot, a half-remembered brief. Read all of it,\nwrite in what you can with `proposal_start`, then report:\n\n    قرأت مما أرسلت:\n      العميل    الأستاذ فهد الفلاني · 055 123 4567\n      المشروع   فيلا سكنية · الخبر · الثقبة\n      الأرض     386.15 م² · قطعة 1 · مخطط 42\n      بلدي      13 من 15 قيمة\n\n    ما زال ناقصاً:\n      قيمتان من بلدي: معامل كتلة البناء, يمكن اضافة دور\n      المتطلبات المساحية\n      الخدمات المشمولة\n      الأتعاب وتقسيم الدفعات\n\nThat report is the interface. It tells them how far along they are and what\none thing to go and find next. `proposal_set` returns exactly this, under\n`ask_next`, grouped by the one place each group is answered from.\n\nAsk by source, never field by field. Somebody looking at one بلدي page can\nanswer fifteen questions at once; being asked them one at a time is\npunishing.\n\n## The rule that matters most\n\n**Never invent a regulatory value.**\n\nBuilding ratio, setbacks, floor count, maximum height, use code, plot area,\nplot number, plan number. These come from بلدي or from the deed, and they go\nonto page 4, which is a restatement of what the municipality says about\nsomebody's land. A plausible-looking 2 metre side setback that you filled in\nto be helpful is a professional liability, not a convenience.\n\nIf you do not have one, leave it out. The page prints empty space, the\nreview names it, and that is the correct outcome.\n\nEverything else you may propose, as long as you show your work: «الخبر →\nKhobar» saves them typing. A setback does not.\n\n### When they ask for a stand-in anyway\n\nThey will, and they are right to. A page full of gaps cannot be judged for\nlayout, and reviewing the design is real work that should not wait for a\nmunicipality.\n\nSo fill it, and make the fill impossible to mistake later:\n\n    proposal_set({ job_id, fields: { farratio: \"غير محدد\" },\n                   estimated: [\"farratio\"] })\n\n**In the same call.** A value written now and marked later is a value that\nwas unmarked for a while, and the read-back in between said it was a fact.\n\nA marked value prints «تقريبًا» beside it on the page, so the client is told\ntoo, and it is named in every review until somebody clears it with\n`confirmed`.\n\nThe danger is specific: `{{farratio}}` on a slide is obviously unfinished.\n`غير محدد` on a slide is obviously fine, right up until a client acts on it.\n\n## What you must never ask for\n\nThese already exist somewhere in the answers, and asking again creates a\nsecond copy that can disagree with the first.\n\n| Never ask | Where it comes from |\n|---|---|\n| the fee in Arabic words | spelled from the figure on every render |\n| the one-line brief on page 4 | counted off the storeys in the brief on page 5 |\n| which phases appear | the services sold |\n| the bars on the Gantt chart | the durations |\n| how wide the chart grid is | the length of the work |\n| «القطعة رقم (27)» on page 5 | the plot number |\n| today's date, the fourteen-day validity | filled by `proposal_start` |\n| page numbers, which rail square is lit | the deck works them out |\n\nEight of the fifteen pages need nothing at all: 2, 6, 7, 9, 10, 13, 14, 15.\nThey are studio boilerplate. If somebody asks to change wording on one, say\nout loud that the next twenty clients get the change too, and that it is an\nedit to the deck project rather than to this proposal.\n\n## The three decisions\n\n**Services.** Ask every time. No default, no guess from the project type.\nShow all eleven as a numbered list (read them from `vado://services`) and\ntake the answer. Whatever is named prints in ink on page 8; everything else\nprints N/A in grey. It decides what the fee buys, what page 9 promises and\nwhat page 11 schedules. A preset here would let somebody ship a proposal\nwhose commercial terms were never actually decided.\n\n**The fee and the split.** `costnumber` excludes VAT. The house default is\n30/30/30/10. A payment is three parts and nothing else: the word in front of\nthe event, the event, and the share. Send them together:\n\n    payments: [\n      { when: \"adv\",    event_ar: \"عند قبول هذا العرض وتوقيع العقد\", pct: 30 },\n      { when: \"after\",  event_ar: \"موافقة المالك على التصميم المبدئي\", pct: 30 },\n      { when: \"after\",  event_ar: \"اكتمال الرسوم التنفيذية\",          pct: 30 },\n      { when: \"before\", event_ar: \"جدول الكميات والمواصفات\",          pct: 10 }\n    ]\n\nThe heading the client reads and the sentence with the riyal amount under it\nare both built from those three, so a payment cannot say one thing above and\nanother below. Read the amounts back: a wrong share is spotted as a wrong\nriyal figure, never as a percentage nobody multiplied.\n\n**Architecture zone and level.** Closed lists of twenty and four, in\n`vado://lists`. For the Eastern Province the zone is nearly always عمارة\nالساحل الشرقي, and عمارة القطيف or عمارة واحات الأحساء for those areas.\nPropose; do not assume. A value not on the list is refused.\n\n## The brief on page 5\n\nThis page has **no fixed shape**, and it is the page most likely to carry the\nlast client's villa into this one. Ask what the project actually has.\n\nA villa has outdoor spaces and floors. A fuel station has a forecourt,\nbuildings and utilities. An office block has levels and a core. A mosque has\na prayer hall and ablutions.\n\n    spatial: { groups: [\n      { title_ar: \"المساحات الخارجية\", items: [\"موقف 3 سيارات\", \"حديقة\"] },\n      { title_ar: \"المساحات الداخلية\", blocks: [\n        { name_ar: \"الدور الأرضي\", contents_ar: \"مجلس , صالة معيشة , مطبخ\" },\n        { name_ar: \"الدور الأول\",  contents_ar: \"غرفة نوم رئيسية (ماستر) , ثلاث غرف نوم\" }\n      ] }\n    ] }\n\nThe client checks this page first, because it is the only one about their own\nhouse.\n\n## The site map\n\nPage 4 carries a picture of the plot, and there is no way to send one\nthrough this connector: it is chosen, cropped and faded in the browser. Mark\nit as a stand-in so nobody forgets:\n\n    proposal_set({ job_id, estimated: [\"map\"] })\n\nThe review then names «صورة الموقع» every time, and the deck says «الصفحة\nتعرض صورة مؤقتة» until the employee replaces it on page 4.\n\n## Durations\n\nAsk for these every time, in days, one number per phase, against the list in\n`vado://phases`. They are the most project-specific thing in the deck after\nthe price: a villa's technical drawings take 45 days, a mixed-use block's\ntake three times that.\n\n    كم يوماً لكل مرحلة؟\n      CD  التصميم المعماري المبدئي   لوحة الأفكار ٧  +  المخططات ٢١\n      DD  تطوير التصميم              ٧\n      TD  الرسومات التنفيذية         ٤٥\n      GA  إصدار رخصة البناء          ٧\n      TD  المواصفات والكميات         ١٤\n\nThe number is the only thing needed. Bar length, where a bar starts, the\ndashed drops between phases and how many weeks the grid holds are all\ncomputed. A phase left with no duration is drawn with an empty cell and no\nbar, which a client reads as work with no end date, so the review names it.\n\n## Before you hand it over\n\nRun `proposal_review` and **print the read-back**. Do not summarise it away.\n\nA machine can tell you a field is empty. Only the person who knows the\nproject can tell you the plot number is the neighbour's, and they can only do\nthat if you show it to them.\n\nThe review returns four things that stop nothing but must be said:\n\n* `missing`: prints as empty space on the page\n* `blocking`: the file disagrees with itself. A split that misses 100, a\n  written price that does not match the figure, a scope still promising a\n  service page 8 marks N/A\n* `estimated`: reads correctly and may be wrong\n* `regulatory_stated_as_read`: every بلدي value not marked تقريبي, listed\n  every single time, because nothing here can tell a value read off بلدي\n  from one somebody made up\n\nNothing refuses to produce the file. A proposal goes out while a بلدي number\nis still being chased, and a tool that refuses to print gets worked around by\nsomebody rebuilding the deck by hand, which is how a proposal leaves with no\ncheck at all. Say what is open, then hand it over.\n\n## Handing it over\n\n`proposal_finish` returns a link. Give it to them plainly:\n\n    جاهز. افتح العرض من هنا:\n    https://vado-tfp.vercel.app/?job=…\n\n    يطلب كلمة مرور المكتب مرة واحدة.\n    اقرأ صفحة ٥ (الغرف) وصفحة ١٢ (الأتعاب) بعينك، ثم اضغط «قبل الإرسال»\n    ثم «حمّل الـ PDF».\n\n    ما زال مفتوحاً: قيمتان تقريبيتان (معامل كتلة البناء, يمكن اضافة دور).\n\nThe last step is theirs, and it is theirs on purpose: the browser prints the\nPDF with the real fonts embedded, and a human looks at fifteen pages before a\nclient does.\n\n## Amending\n\n«ارفع السعر إلى ٢٥٬٠٠٠ على عرض فهد» is a normal request. `proposal_list` to\nfind it, `proposal_get` to read it, `proposal_set` to change it,\n`proposal_review`, then say what changed. Keep the same `tfp_number` unless a\nnew revision is asked for; if it is, start a new proposal and keep both,\nbecause the client may still be holding the first one.\n\n## Two things that are not your call\n\n**The scope pages (6 and 7) are the studio's words.** You may say what looks\nwrong with them for this job. You may not rewrite them. If the scope promises\na service page 8 marks N/A, the review says so and a human settles it.\n\n**A project that is not residential.** The scope was written around a\nresidential building: concept design, municipal approval, then technical\ndrawings across architecture, structure, mechanical and electrical. A fuel\nstation needs ARAMCO and civil defence. An interior fit-out has no structural\ndiscipline at all. Name what looks wrong and let them decide.\n"},{"id":"what-to-ask","title":"ما يُسأل عنه","why":"The eight questions, and everything that must never be asked because the deck already knows it.","text":"# What to ask for, and what never to ask for\n\nFifteen slides. **Eight questions.** Eight slides need nothing at all.\n\nKnowing which is which is most of the job. Asking for something the deck\nalready knows wastes the user's time and invites a second version of a fact\nthat is already recorded somewhere else.\n\n## The seven\n\nAsk these in this order. Each one is a single source, so a person can\nanswer the whole group from one place.\n\n| # | Ask for | Feeds | Where they get it |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Who and what** — client name, phone, email, project type, city, district | cover, letter, contract | their phone, the WhatsApp thread |\n| 2 | **The land** — area, source, plot number, plan number | slide 4 | the deed or the survey |\n| 3 | **The location** — coordinates, national address, Maps link, and a map image | slide 4 | Google Maps, سبل |\n| 4 | **Balady** — the 15 regulatory values | slide 4 | بلدي, المستكشف الجغرافي |\n| 5 | **Architecture** — Saudi zone, level, style | slide 4 | the architecture map, and a design decision |\n| 6 | **The brief** — the rooms or parts, grouped | slide 5 | the kickoff meeting |\n| 7 | **The deal** — which services, the fee, the payment split | slides 8, 9, 12 | the person pricing it |\n| 8 | **How long each phase takes**, in days | slides 9 and 11 | whoever is programming the job |\n\n## What follows on its own\n\nNever ask for any of these. They already exist somewhere in the answers\nabove, and asking again creates a second copy that can disagree.\n\n| Not asked | Comes from |\n|---|---|\n| `costwritten` | the fee, spelled in Arabic by the build |\n| `spatialneeds` | counted off the brief's floors |\n| The phases on slide 9 | the services sold |\n| The bars on the Gantt | the durations, so they cannot disagree |\n| How wide the chart grid is | the length of the work |\n| The legend codes | the phases actually on the page |\n| `القطعة رقم (27)` on slide 5 | `lotnumber` |\n| The English name, city, district, title | proposed from the Arabic, then confirmed |\n| `date` | today |\n| `tfp_dur` | 14 unless told otherwise |\n| Page numbers | live fields, they renumber themselves |\n| Which rail square is lit | the section the page belongs to |\n\n## The eight slides nobody fills\n\n2 contents · 6 and 7 scope · 9 phases · 10 method · 11 timeline ·\n13 agreement · 14 contact · 15 closing.\n\nThey are studio boilerplate in `content.json`. Changing one is a studio\ndecision that affects every future proposal, not a per-job edit. If someone\nasks to change wording on these pages, say that out loud before doing it:\nthe next twenty clients get the change too.\n\nThe exceptions are small and automatic. Slide 13 picks up the validity\nperiod, the project type and the client name. Slide 10 picks up the\narchitectural style, one word, and is otherwise entirely fixed: it is the\nstudio arguing how it designs, and it says nothing about any particular\nproject.\n\n## How the answers arrive\n\nDo not run a questionnaire. Open with \"send me whatever you have\" and read\nit. People arrive with a WhatsApp thread, a photo of a deed, a Balady\nscreenshot, a half-remembered brief. Extract everything you can, then\nreport what you got and what is still missing, grouped.\n\nThat report is the interface. It tells them how far along they are and what\none thing to go and find next.\n\nFor the fifteen Balady values, take any of three routes and say so: a\npasted block, a screenshot, or one at a time using the Arabic labels. See\n`balady.md`.\n\n## Durations\n\nAsk for these every time, in days, one number per phase. They are the most\nproject-specific thing in the deck after the price: a villa's technical\ndrawings take 45 days, a mixed-use block's take three times that.\n\nRead the phases out of `content.json` and ask against them, using whatever\nthe last similar job took as the opening number rather than a blank:\n\n```\nHow long for each phase, in days?\n\n  CD  التصميم المعماري المبدئي   mood board 7  +  drawings 21\n  DD  تطوير التصميم              7\n  TD  الرسومات التنفيذية         45\n  GA  إصدار رخصة البناء          7\n  TD  المواصفات والكميات         14\n```\n\nThe number is the only thing you need. The bar length, where the bar\nstarts, the dashed drops between phases and how many weeks the grid holds\nare all computed from it. Change TD from 45 to 90 and the project goes from\n83 days to 128, the chart from 12 weeks to 20, and every later phase slides\nright on its own.\n\nTwo phases do not simply follow the one before, and those rules live in\n`phases.rows[].schedule`, not in the answer you collect:\n\n* `overlap_days` — the licence phase starts 18 days before the technical\n  drawings finish, because it is submitted off drawings in progress\n* `parallel: true` — draws the double arrow that marks work running\n  alongside another phase\n\nIf someone wants those changed, that is a studio decision about how VADO\nruns a job, not a per-proposal answer.\n\n## The one question that is always asked\n\nWhich services. Every proposal, no default, no guess by project type. Show\nall eleven and take the answer. It decides what the fee buys, what slide 9\npromises, and what slide 11 schedules. A preset would let somebody ship a\nproposal whose commercial terms were never actually decided.\n"},{"id":"fields","title":"الحقول","why":"Every field: its Arabic label, where the value comes from, its format and a real example.","text":"# The 49 fields\n\nGrouped by where the value comes from, because that is how a human answers\nthem. Ask one group at a time.\n\nThe Arabic label is what appears on the source document or the screen, so\nuse it in the prompt. The example is real-shaped, not a placeholder.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [Reference](#1-reference) — 3 fields, from the tracker\n2. [Client](#2-client) — 8 fields, from the contact\n3. [Project](#3-project) — 7 fields, from the kickoff meeting\n4. [Land](#4-land) — 4 fields, from the deed or survey\n5. [Location](#5-location) — 3 fields, from Google Maps and سبل\n6. [Balady limits](#6-balady-limits) — 15 fields, one source, one paste\n7. [Architecture](#7-architecture) — 3 fields, two closed lists\n8. [Money](#8-money) — 6 fields, a decision\n9. [Services](#9-services) — not fields; a list of ids\n10. [Rooms](#10-rooms) — not fields; the slide 5 schedule\n\n---\n\n## 1. Reference\n\n| Field | Arabic | Source | Format | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `tfp_number` | رقم العرض | Tracker sheet, or derive | `YYMMDD` + initials + type code | `250402MKM-RES-VILLA` |\n| `date` | التاريخ | Today | `D MMM YYYY`, month in caps | `23 AUG 2026` |\n| `tfp_dur` | الصلاحية | House standard | plain number of days | `14` |\n\n`tfp_dur` appears twice: on the cover as the validity, and in note 1 on\nslide 13 as the period the offer stands. One number, two places.\n\nType codes seen in the wild: `RES-VILLA`. The rest are a guess, so propose\nand let it be corrected: `RES-BLDG`, `COM-BLDG`, `ADM-OFFICE`, `FUEL-STN`.\n\n## 2. Client\n\n| Field | Arabic | Format | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `client_company_ar` | اسم الشركة | leave empty for a private client | `شركة الفلاني القابضة` |\n| `name_title_ar` | اللقب | السيد, الأستاذ, الدكتور, المهندس | `الأستاذ` |\n| `firstname_ar` | الاسم الأول | | `فهد` |\n| `lastname_ar` | اسم العائلة | الفلاني, أبافلان, آل فلان, بافلان | `الفلاني` |\n| `name_title` | title | Mr., Dr., Eng. | `Mr.` |\n| `firstname` | first name | | `Fahad` |\n| `lastname` | last name | **space after Al** | `Al Mulla`, not `AlMulla` |\n| `phone` | الجوال | KSA format | `055 123 4567` |\n| `email` | البريد | | `fahad@example.com` |\n\nThe Arabic name lands on the cover, the letter opening on slide 3, and the\nsignature block on slide 13.\n\n`client_company_ar` is for a client that is a company. Filled, it prints\nabove the person's name in the الطرف الأول block on slide 13, the way the\nstudio's own company prints above its signatory opposite. Left empty, no\nline is drawn and a private client's block reads exactly as it always has.\n\nThe English set (`name_title`, `firstname`, `lastname`, and the Latin\nproject, city and district) is not printed anywhere at present. The English\nblock it fed on the cover was removed when the deck went fully Arabic. The\nfields are kept because the tracker maps to them and the English edition\nwill want them back.\n\n## 3. Project\n\n| Field | Arabic | Notes | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `project_type_ar` | نوعية المشروع | | `فيلا سكنية` |\n| `project_type` | project type | | `Residential Villa` |\n| `city_ar` | المدينة | | `الخبر` |\n| `city` | city | | `Khobar` |\n| `district_ar` | الحي | | `الثقبة` |\n| `district` | district | | `Al Thuqbah` |\n| `spatialneeds` | المتطلبات المساحية | one line, Arabic | `فيلا سكنية مفصولة` |\n\n`spatialneeds` is the one-line summary on slide 4. The detailed room list is\nseparate; see [Rooms](#10-rooms).\n\n`project_type_ar` also appears inside the contract paragraph on slide 13,\nso it must read naturally in a sentence: `لمشروع فيلا سكنية للطرف الأول`.\n\n## 4. Land\n\n| Field | Arabic | Source | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `lotarea` | مساحة الأرض | Deed or survey, m² as a number | `386.15` |\n| `areasource` | مصدر المساحة | الصك / الرفع المساحي / المستكشف | `الصك` |\n| `lotnumber` | رقم القطعة | Deed | `1` |\n| `districtnumber` | رقم المخطط | Deed | `42` |\n\n## 5. Location\n\n| Field | Arabic | Source | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `coordinates` | الاحداثيات | Google Maps | `26.2794, 50.2083` |\n| `nat_address` | العنوان الوطني | سبل (Saudi Post) | `RAKA2345, 7639 - 34413` |\n| `googlelink` | رابط الموقع | Google Maps share link | `https://maps.app.goo.gl/...` |\n\nThese three print very small (4–5 pt) inside the location cell on slide 4.\nThey are there for the record, not to be read across a table.\n\n## 6. Balady limits\n\nFifteen fields, one source: بلدي or المستكشف الجغرافي لأمانة المنطقة الشرقية.\nGet them in one go. See `balady.md` for parsing.\n\n| Field | Arabic label on the source | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| `usecode` | رمز الاستخدام | `س-1-أ سكني` |\n| `divtype` | نوع التقسيم | `لايوجد` |\n| `divdesc` | وصف التقسيم | `لايوجد` |\n| `landuse` | الاستخدام لقطعة الأرض | `سكني` |\n| `usedesc` | وصف اشتراط البناء | `سكني بنسبة 60% من مساحة الارض بارتفاع عدد 2 طابق بحد اقصى 10 متر` |\n| `numberofunits` | عدد الوحدات | `وحدة واحدة بالقطعة` |\n| `buildingratio` | نسبة البناء | `0.6` |\n| `minimumelev` | الحد الأدنى للواجهة | `20` |\n| `frontsetback` | ارتداد الواجهة | `1/5 عرض الشارع` |\n| `sidesetback` | ارتداد الجوانب | `2` |\n| `backsetback` | ارتداد خلفي | `2` |\n| `floors` | الطوابق | `2` |\n| `height` | ارتفاع الطابق | `10` |\n| `canaddfloor` | يمكن اضافة دور | `لا` |\n| `farratio` | معامل كتلة البناء | `غير محدد` |\n\nNote the shapes. Setbacks are sometimes a number in metres and sometimes a\nrule (`1/5 عرض الشارع`). `farratio` is often `غير محدد`. `canaddfloor` is\nنعم or لا. Do not normalise these into something tidier than the source:\nthe client may compare the page against Balady.\n\n`usecode` appears twice on slide 4, in two different tables. One field\nfeeds both.\n\n## 7. Architecture\n\n| Field | Arabic | Source | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ksaarchzone` | تصنيف العمارة السعودية | Closed list of 20 | `عمارة الساحل الشرقي` |\n| `ksaarchlevel` | مستوى العمارة السعودية | Closed list of 4 | `مستوى 3 (معاصر, انتقالي, تقليدي)` |\n| `archstyle` | الطراز المعماري | Design decision | `معاصر` |\n\nThe two lists live in `~/dev/vado-tfp/content.json` under `lists`. Read them\nfrom there. `presend.py` validates against the same lists, so a value you\ninvent will be blocked, correctly.\n\nFor the Eastern Province the zone is nearly always `عمارة الساحل الشرقي`,\nand `عمارة القطيف` or `عمارة واحات الأحساء` for those areas. Propose, do\nnot assume.\n\n## 8. Money\n\n| Field | Arabic | Notes | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `costnumber` | التكلفة رقمًا | Excluding VAT | `25,000` |\n| `costwritten` | التكلفة كتابةً | Set to `\"auto\"` | `auto` |\n| `p1` | الدفعة الأولى | On signature | `30%` |\n| `p2` | الدفعة الثانية | On concept approval | `30%` |\n| `p3` | الدفعة الثالثة | On technical drawings | `30%` |\n| `p4` | الدفعة الرابعة | Before the BOQ | `10%` |\n\n`costwritten: \"auto\"` makes the build spell the figure in Arabic words, the\njob the Excel macro used to do. Override it only if the client wants\ndifferent wording.\n\nThe four percentages must total 100. The build refuses otherwise, because a\npayment schedule that does not add up is the kind of error that costs a\nsignature.\n\nNote: `30%` in a right-to-left paragraph renders as `%30`. That is a known\nopen question on this deck, not a bug you introduced.\n\n## 9. Services\n\nNot fields. The job file carries a list of ids; everything not listed is\nmarked N/A on slide 8, and the included ones are stacked first in dark ink.\n\n| id | English | Arabic |\n|---|---|---|\n| `concept` | Architectural Conceptual Design | التصميم المعماري المبدئي |\n| `engineering` | Architectural + Engineering Design | التصميم الهندسي والمخططات التنفيذية |\n| `permit` | Municipal Permit | إصدار رخصة البناء |\n| `landscape` | Landscape Design | تصميم البيئة المبنية (لاندسكيب) |\n| `interior` | Interior Design | التصميم الداخلي |\n| `bidding` | Bidding Management | إدارة الطرح والمناقصات |\n| `supervision` | Supervision | الإشراف الهندسي |\n| `pm` | Project Management | إدارة المشروع |\n| `bim` | BIM Services | خدمات النمذجة المعلوماتية المعمارية |\n| `archviz` | Architectural Visualization | الإظهار المعماري التسويقي |\n| `hbu` | Highest and Best Use Study | الدراسة العقارية والاستخدام الأمثل |\n\n### Which ones to include\n\nAsk. Every time, for every proposal.\n\nThere is no default set and no suggestion by project type. A preset here\nwould look helpful and would quietly let somebody ship a proposal whose\nservices were never actually decided, and the services are what the fee\nbuys. Show all eleven as a numbered list, take the answer, write the ids.\n\nEverything not named becomes N/A. That is the point of the page: the greyed\nrows are the boundary, and a client who wanted landscape can see it was not\nincluded rather than assuming it was.\n\n### The old Excel names\n\nEach service carries `alias_excel`, the wording the old form used, because\na tracker sheet keyed on those strings still has to reconcile. The deck\nsays `Architectural + Engineering Design`; the Excel said `Engineering\nDesign`. Same service, both names recorded.\n\n### Room on the page\n\nEleven rows today, and fourteen fit above the footer. `presend.py` blocks\npast fourteen.\n\n## 10. The brief on slide 5\n\nNot fields. **This page has no fixed shape.** A villa has outdoor spaces\nand floors. A fuel station has a forecourt, buildings and utilities. An\noffice block has levels and a core. A mosque has a prayer hall and\nablutions. Do not force a project into the villa's shape because the\ntemplate started there.\n\nThe model is a list of groups. A group has a title and holds either a flat\nlist of `items`, or `blocks` that each name a part and say what is inside\nit, or both. Any number of groups, any number of blocks, in whatever order\nthe project wants.\n\n```json\n\"spatial\": {\n  \"groups\": [\n    { \"title_ar\": \"المساحات الخارجية\",\n      \"items\": [\"موقف 3 سيارات\", \"حديقة\"] },\n    { \"title_ar\": \"المساحات الداخلية\",\n      \"blocks\": [\n        { \"name_ar\": \"الدور الأرضي\", \"contents_ar\": \"مجلس , صالة معيشة , مطبخ\" },\n        { \"name_ar\": \"الدور الأول\",  \"contents_ar\": \"غرفة نوم رئيسية (ماستر) , ثلاث غرف نوم\" }\n      ] }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### The same page, a fuel station\n\n```json\n\"groups\": [\n  { \"title_ar\": \"الساحة الأمامية\",\n    \"items\": [\"6 مضخات وقود\", \"مظلة معدنية\", \"خزانات أرضية\"] },\n  { \"title_ar\": \"المباني\", \"blocks\": [\n      { \"name_ar\": \"مبنى الخدمات\", \"contents_ar\": \"بقالة , مقهى , دورات مياه , مصلى\" },\n      { \"name_ar\": \"المغسلة\",      \"contents_ar\": \"خطان للغسيل , غرفة معدات\" } ] },\n  { \"title_ar\": \"المرافق الخارجية\",\n    \"items\": [\"مواقف زوار\", \"غرفة كهرباء\", \"حاويات نفايات\"] }\n]\n```\n\n### Shapes worth reaching for\n\n| Project | Groups that usually fit |\n|---|---|\n| فيلا سكنية | المساحات الخارجية (items) · المساحات الداخلية (blocks per floor) |\n| عمارة سكنية | الأدوار (blocks per floor) · الخدمات المشتركة (items) · المواقف (items) |\n| عمارة استثمارية | الدور التجاري (block) · الأدوار السكنية (blocks) · الخدمات (items) |\n| مكاتب ادارية | الأدوار (blocks) · المنطقة العامة (items) · الخدمات الفنية (items) |\n| محطة وقود | الساحة الأمامية (items) · المباني (blocks) · المرافق الخارجية (items) |\n| مسجد | المصلى (block) · الملحقات (blocks) · الساحات (items) |\n| مستودع | صالة التخزين (block) · المكاتب (block) · الساحات والمناورة (items) |\n\nThese are starting points, not a menu. Ask what the project actually\nhas and build the groups from the answer.\n\n### Writing the contents\n\n`contents_ar` is one comma-separated sentence per block, because that is\nhow the page is set. Room names are written plainly; the slide applies the\nindentation from `spatial.indent`, three numbers in `content.json`.\n\n### What follows from it\n\n`spatialneeds` on slide 4 can be counted off this page when the brief is\norganised by storeys: two blocks named دور plus one named ملحق produce\n`فيلا سكنية دورين وملحق علوي`. Set the field to `\"auto\"` and it follows the\nrooms.\n\nWhen the brief has no storeys, as with a fuel station, no sentence of that\nshape describes it. The build says so rather than inventing one, leaves the\ntag showing, and `presend.py` blocks. Write the summary by hand in those\ncases.\n\nThis is the page that carries the last client's villa into this one if\nnobody asks. Ask.\n"},{"id":"balady","title":"قراءة بيانات بلدي","why":"How to read pasted or photographed بلدي plot data, and what never to tidy up in it.","text":"# Reading Balady plot data\n\nFifteen of the 49 fields come from one place: بلدي or المستكشف الجغرافي\nلأمانة المنطقة الشرقية. Getting them in one move instead of fifteen is the\nsingle biggest saving in the whole workflow.\n\nAccept whatever arrives. Three routes, in order of how much you should\ntrust yourself.\n\n## Route 1: pasted text\n\nMost reliable. He copies the plot panel and pastes it. Match on the Arabic\nlabel, not on position: the panel reorders between views.\n\n| Look for | Field | Watch for |\n|---|---|---|\n| رمز الاستخدام | `usecode` | keep the whole string, e.g. `س-1-أ سكني` |\n| نوع التقسيم | `divtype` | often `لايوجد` |\n| وصف التقسيم | `divdesc` | often `لايوجد` |\n| الاستخدام / الاستخدام لقطعة الأرض | `landuse` | e.g. `سكني` |\n| وصف اشتراط البناء / الاشتراط | `usedesc` | a whole sentence, keep it whole |\n| عدد الوحدات | `numberofunits` | a phrase, not a number: `وحدة واحدة بالقطعة` |\n| نسبة البناء | `buildingratio` | `60%` and `0.6` both appear. Keep the source form |\n| الحد الأدنى للواجهة / الحد الأدنى لعرض الواجهة | `minimumelev` | metres |\n| ارتداد الواجهة / الارتداد الأمامي | `frontsetback` | may be a rule: `1/5 عرض الشارع` |\n| ارتداد الجوانب / الارتداد الجانبي | `sidesetback` | metres, or `لايوجد` |\n| ارتداد خلفي / الارتداد الخلفي | `backsetback` | metres, or `لايوجد` |\n| عدد الأدوار / الطوابق | `floors` | a count |\n| ارتفاع المبنى / ارتفاع الطابق | `height` | metres. The label says طابق but the value is usually the whole building |\n| يمكن اضافة دور / إضافة دور | `canaddfloor` | `نعم` or `لا` |\n| معامل كتلة البناء / معامل البناء / FAR | `farratio` | often `غير محدد` |\n\nAfter parsing, report what you got and what you did not:\n\n```\nRead 13 of 15 from the Balady text.\nCould not find: معامل كتلة البناء, يمكن اضافة دور\n\n  رمز الاستخدام      س-1-أ سكني\n  نسبة البناء         60%\n  الطوابق             2\n  ...\n\nTwo questions rather than fifteen.\n```\n\n## Route 2: a screenshot\n\nThey drop an image. You can read it, but Arabic numerals and thin table\nrules are exactly where reading goes wrong, and a misread setback reaches\na client as a professional statement.\n\nSo: read it, then show **every** value back as a table and ask for a\nconfirmation or a correction before anything is written. Not a summary. The table.\n\nSay why you are asking: \"screenshots are where I misread digits, so read\nthese back to me before I write them.\"\n\n## Route 3: one at a time\n\nThey are on the phone, or the panel will not copy. Use the Arabic label from\nthe table above as the prompt, in the order the Balady panel shows them, so\nthey can read straight down the screen. Do not translate the label into\nEnglish: they are looking at Arabic.\n\n## Do not tidy the values\n\n`60%` and `0.6`. `1/5 عرض الشارع` and `2`. `غير محدد` and blank. The\ntemptation is to normalise these into a clean schema. Resist it. Slide 4 is\na restatement of what the municipality says, and a client or a reviewer may\nhold the page next to the Balady screen. A value that reads differently\nfrom the source looks like an error even when the arithmetic is identical.\n\nThe one exception: strip surrounding whitespace and stray colons.\n\n## The footnote on slide 4\n\nThe page carries a standing note that the data is from المستكشف الجغرافي\nand the 2026 residential building requirements, correct as at the date of\nthe proposal. That is why `date` matters here and not only on the cover: it\nis the date the regulatory snapshot was taken. If the plot data is more\nthan a few weeks old, say so and offer to refresh it.\n"},{"id":"arabic-english","title":"العربية والإنجليزية","why":"Arabic to English for titles, cities, districts and project types.","text":"# Arabic to English, for the cover\n\nSix fields on the cover exist in both scripts. The Arabic is authoritative;\nthe English is a courtesy line under it. Propose the English from these\ntables and let the user correct it. Never silently substitute.\n\nTransliteration is a matter of taste and VADO has a house habit: **Al with\na space**, no hyphen. `Al Mulla`, `Al Thuqbah`, `Al Ahsa`. The old Excel\nform called this out explicitly, so it is a rule someone got burned by.\n\n## Titles\n\n| Arabic | English |\n|---|---|\n| السيد | Mr. |\n| الأستاذ | Mr. |\n| السيدة | Mrs. |\n| الآنسة | Ms. |\n| الدكتور | Dr. |\n| الدكتورة | Dr. |\n| المهندس | Eng. |\n| المهندسة | Eng. |\n| الشيخ | Sheikh |\n| الأمير | Prince |\n| الأميرة | Princess |\n\n## Cities\n\nVADO works the Eastern Province, so these come up constantly.\n\n| Arabic | English |\n|---|---|\n| الخبر | Khobar |\n| الدمام | Dammam |\n| الظهران | Dhahran |\n| الأحساء | Al Ahsa |\n| الهفوف | Hofuf |\n| المبرز | Mubarraz |\n| القطيف | Qatif |\n| سيهات | Sayhat |\n| صفوى | Safwa |\n| الجبيل | Jubail |\n| رأس تنورة | Ras Tanura |\n| بقيق | Abqaiq |\n| النعيرية | Nairyah |\n| الخفجي | Khafji |\n| حفر الباطن | Hafar Al Batin |\n| الرياض | Riyadh |\n| جدة | Jeddah |\n| مكة المكرمة | Makkah |\n| المدينة المنورة | Madinah |\n\n## Districts\n\nKhobar and Dammam districts, where most of the work is.\n\n| Arabic | English |\n|---|---|\n| الثقبة | Al Thuqbah |\n| الكورنيش | Al Corniche |\n| العليا | Al Olaya |\n| البندرية | Al Bandariyah |\n| الحزام الأخضر | Green Belt |\n| اليرموك | Al Yarmouk |\n| الراكة | Ar Rakah |\n| الخزامى | Al Khuzama |\n| الجسر | Al Jisr |\n| العقربية | Al Aqrabiyah |\n| الشراع | Ash Shira'a |\n| الحمراء | Al Hamra |\n| التحلية | Al Tahliah |\n| الأندلس | Al Andalus |\n| إشبيليا | Ishbiliyah |\n| المها | Al Maha |\n| الصواري | As Sawari |\n| اللؤلؤ | Al Lulu |\n| الخبر الشمالية | North Khobar |\n| الخبر الجنوبية | South Khobar |\n| الشاطئ | Al Shatea |\n| الفيصلية | Al Faisaliyah |\n| النزهة | Al Nuzhah |\n| الروضة | Al Rawdah |\n\nA district not on this list is normal. Propose a transliteration following\nthe same habit and flag that you are guessing.\n\n## Project types\n\n| Arabic | English |\n|---|---|\n| فيلا سكنية | Residential Villa |\n| فيلا دوبلكس | Duplex Villa |\n| قصر | Palace |\n| استراحة | Rest House |\n| عمارة سكنية | Residential Building |\n| عمارة استثمارية | Investment Building |\n| مجمع سكني | Residential Compound |\n| مكاتب ادارية | Administrative Offices |\n| مجمع تجاري | Commercial Complex |\n| معرض | Showroom |\n| مستودع | Warehouse |\n| محطة وقود | Fuel Station |\n| مطعم | Restaurant |\n| مقهى | Cafe |\n| مسجد | Mosque |\n| مدرسة | School |\n| عيادة | Clinic |\n| فندق | Hotel |\n\n`project_type_ar` is also dropped into a sentence in the contract on slide\n13: `... لأعمال التصميم المعماري والهندسي لمشروع <type> للطرف الأول ...`.\nCheck it reads naturally there. `فيلا سكنية` does. A type ending in a\nconstruct state may not.\n"},{"id":"deck","title":"الصفحات","why":"What each of the fifteen pages is for, which fields feed it, and which pages carry risk.","text":"# What each slide does, and what feeds it\n\nFifteen slides, A3 portrait, right to left. Knowing what a page is *for*\ntells you which questions actually matter, and which gap is worth blocking\na send over.\n\nThe deck argues a case in four movements: **who we are** (1–3), **what we\nunderstand about your plot** (4–5), **what we will do** (6–11), **what it\ncosts and what you are agreeing to** (12–15).\n\n| # | Page | Purpose | Fed by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Cover | Names the client, the project and the offer. The only page with both scripts. | client, project, `tfp_number`, `date`, `tfp_dur` |\n| 2 | المحتوى | Contents. The eight sections here drive the square rail on every later page. | fixed |\n| 3 | المقدمة | The covering letter, signed. Establishes VADO's history and values. | `name_title_ar`, `firstname_ar`, `lastname_ar`, `signatory` |\n| 4 | عن المشروع | **The credibility page.** Restates the plot back to the client: area, plot number, coordinates, and the fifteen municipal limits. Says \"we have read your land.\" | land, location, Balady, architecture zone |\n| 5 | نطاق العمل | The room schedule. The client checks this first, because it is the only page about *their* house. | `spatial` |\n| 6 | نطاق العمل | Scope, phase one: concept design and the initial municipal approval. | fixed |\n| 7 | نطاق العمل | Scope, phase two: technical drawings across all disciplines, then the licence. The longest page. | fixed |\n| 8 | نطاق العمل | **The commercial boundary.** Eleven services, marked in or N/A. What the fee does and does not buy. | `services` |\n| 9 | نطاق العمل | Phases and deliverables. What arrives, in what format. | fixed |\n| 10 | منهجية العمل | Design method: intent, function, form. The soft-sell page. **Fixed content.** | `archstyle` only |\n| 11 | الخط الزمني | Schedule table plus a Gantt across twelve weeks. | fixed |\n| 12 | العرض المالي | **The price.** Total, in figures and Arabic words, then the four payments and the bank details. | money |\n| 13 | الاتفاقية | Conditions, the contract paragraph, two signature blocks. Signing this page forms the contract. | `tfp_dur`, `project_type_ar`, client name |\n| 14 | معلومات التواصل | Contacts and a QR code. | fixed |\n| 15 | Closing | Tagline. | fixed |\n\n## Who signs\n\n`content.json` has a `signatories` block. Each entry holds the name, the\nprefixed name, the role, the office and the signature image as one record,\nand a job picks one with `\"signatory\": \"mkm\"`. Slides 3 and 13 both read\nit, so the scanned signature and the typed name can never disagree.\n\nOnly `mkm` exists today. Adding a second signer means one new entry and one\nnew PNG in `assets/`, nothing else.\n\n## The pages that carry risk\n\n**Slide 4** is where an invented number does damage. Every value is a\nrestatement of a municipal record. Wrong here is not a typo; it is a claim\nabout someone's land.\n\n**Slide 5** is where staleness does damage. It is prose about a specific\nvilla. Nothing in the build knows whether the rooms belong to this client\nor the last one, which is why the pre-send check nags about it.\n\n**Slide 8** is where ambiguity does damage. A service left marked \"in\" that\nwas not priced is a scope argument three months from now.\n\n**Slide 12** is where arithmetic does damage. The figure and the words must\nagree, and the four payments must total 100. Both are checked, both block.\n\n**Slide 13** is a contract. The `tfp_dur` on it is the period the offer\nstands, and `project_type_ar` sits inside the operative sentence.\n\n## Pages that never change\n\n**Slide 10 is fixed.** It argues how the studio designs and says nothing\nabout any particular project. The only thing on it that moves is\n`{{archstyle}}`, one word. Never ask about this page, never customise it\nper client, and if someone wants its wording changed, say out loud that\nevery future proposal gets the change too.\n\nThe three pillar names on it must match in three places: the triangle, the\nlead paragraph, and the three explanations. They did not, for years: the\ndiagram said الوظيفية while the paragraph explaining it said الوظيفة. If\nyou touch one, touch all three.\n\n6, 7, 9, 11, 14, 15 and most of 2, 3 and 10 are boilerplate in\n`content.json`. Changing one is an edit to the deck project, not to a job\nfile. Say so rather than putting project-specific\nwording into a page that every future client will also receive.\n\n## The furniture\n\nEvery content page carries the same header logo, a pale rule, the section\ntitle, a rail of squares down the right edge marking which of the eight\nsections you are in, and a footer with the CR number, the chamber number,\nthe address and the page number. All of it is drawn by one function, so it\ncannot drift between pages the way it did in the old file.\n"}];
